# `--runtime` installs raw runtime bytecode as it is, and `--storage` seeds a slot. This
# counter reads slot 0, adds one, and writes it back; with the slot seeded at 0x29 the
# trace shows the read and the write.
# REQUIRES: soldb
# RUN: %soldb run 0x6000405060005460010160005500 --runtime --storage 0x0=0x29 --raw --max-steps 12 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# Without a function signature or data the call carries empty calldata, and the raw
# view lists every instruction of the tiny program.
# RUN: %soldb run 0x6000405060005460010160005500 --runtime --json | jq -e '.status == "success" and (.steps | length) == 10 and (.steps[8].snapshot.storage["0x0"] == "0x1")'

# CHECK: Installed runtime code at 0x5fbdb2315678afecb367f032d93f642f64180aa3
# CHECK: SLOAD
# CHECK-SAME: 0x0
# CHECK: SSTORE
# CHECK-SAME: 0x2a
# CHECK: STOP
